WEBVTT

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.980
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.620
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.920
This episode is about Nagi's new Guardian Character, Rhythm!

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.510
Yo, how's it hangin'?

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.320
Yay!

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.380
Yay!

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.910
You're always so enthusiastic, Rhythm!

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.000
We're gonna catch the rhythm too.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.870
And make it cool!

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:21.740
Doki!

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.960
Cool!

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:41.180
If you were to walk so the wind fluttered the edge of your cape,

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:47.570
people would look up at you in quiet admiration.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:54.870
You can say spicy things like "it's not my style," if you want,

00:00:54.870 --> 00:01:01.290
but I know who you really are because I'm your friend!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.160
Stand! Bow!  {these are the two things said by the class rep when the teacher enters at the start of the school day}

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.690
Nice and orderly now!

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:08.530
And once that's done,

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:13.800
it's time to start the school day.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:21.420
I like Mondays because I can see all my friends.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:27.820
There's nothing wrong with being abnormally happy.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:34.990
At lunch break, we have tea in the Royal Garden,

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:42.330
where I tell you all my secrets!

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.680
Oh? Fujisaki-kun's Guardian Character was born?

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.960
Yeah! It happened when those X Eggs appeared yesterday.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.850
I totally wanna meet him!

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:08.030
I sure hope Nagi gets here real soon!

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.610
Sorry, everyone...

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.070
He's here!

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.160
Hey, hey, Nagi, where's your Guardian Character?

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.950
Yo! I'm Rhythm! Nice to meetcha!

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.700
Wow, he looks just like Nagi!

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.320
You think?

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.330
What's the matter? You look kind of beat...  {okay, yes, this pun is not in the original but it's a good translation regardless so why not :) }

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.920
Well, it's Rhythm, you see...

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:42.220
Episode 92
It's Got to Be Cool! Beat Jumper!

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.930
Are you having problems with Rhythm?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:49.500
No, not exactly. It's just that on my way to the Royal Garden...

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.230
Sorry!

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.130
Nice kick!

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.360
Let's join in with them!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.330
Make it cool!  {editor note: This is his catch phrase, obviously... I'm torn between using "It's got to be cool! and "Make it cool!"... former is more literal but latter is shorter and easier... If you decide one way or the other, change all occurrences, please}

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:18.050
Yay!

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:25.950
Look here, Rhythm. Would you please stop Character Changing me without asking first?

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.390
Over there next!

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.100
Yay!

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.030
Now over here!

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:38.440
Tennis!

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.280
Volleyball!

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.330
Judo!

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.820
Yay!

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.900
Please join the baseball team!

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.150
No, the soccer team!

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:52.770
The basketball team had our eye on him first!

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.420
The judo team, please!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.540
Um, well...

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.980
Bye!

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.970
Honestly, it was too much...

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.910
So <i>that's</i> why you were late!

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.280
Rhythm sure has a spirited personality.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.930
He likes to go with the flow.  {more literally "catches the beat well"}

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:15.900
He looks like he's already getting along well with the other Guardian Characters.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.110
Guys, you've got the awesomest groove goin' on!

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.670
Yay!

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.210
Yay!

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:24.370
Yay!

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:26.470
Yay!

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.530
Yay!

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.300
He's quite the flirt.  {this is quite a bit of an interpretation here.  Literally the word used is "karui" = light, but it can be used in a connotation of "a loose woman/man"  Here rima is really using it as a dual meaning between flirt and "light hearted" I think, but considering the context I think this is the meaning that everyone at the table is thinking}

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.610
An unflappable playboy, indeed.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:37.670
Well, what counts is that he's friendly.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.050
Yeah...

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:47.740
It is common courtesy to greet your King first, and yet...

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.570
Heya, Kiseki!

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.570
Ah, finally, there you are.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.060
I am Kiseki, the Guardian Character King!

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.920
Hey! You don't mind sharing your room with Rhythm, right?

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.370
W-What?

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.690
You two will make good roommates-dechu.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:05.460
The King, share his room with a commoner? Preposterous!

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:08.170
But he can't stay with a <i>girl</i>...

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.200
But!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.580
Don't be selfish.  {the usual translation of "cheap" doesn't work here... "selfish" would be okay too, if a little bit off}

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.000
Me, selfish?!

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:16.510
Just calm down.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:18.020
Make it cool, man.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.600
Watch your tongue!

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.670
I don't need a room, dude.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.050
What?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:27.740
This is your pad, man. Just keep usin' it like you always do.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.800
Then we ain't got no problem, yeah?

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.770
So cool!

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.890
He's quite easygoing, unlike a certain someone-dechu...

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.710
I-I...

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.610
He's completely right-nya.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:42.840
You don't need a room to live-nya.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.180
Who's that?

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:50.760
I am the great Yoru! I can smell a kindred free spirit in you-nya.  {He calls himself "ore-sama"... hence}

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.810
They just did a really complicated handshake...

00:05:58.810 --> 00:05:59.890
So cool!

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:02.250
Let me try it, too!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.410
Teach me!

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:11.840
He's way more popular than the "King," don't ya think-nya?

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:20.700
Based on the previous experiment,

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:25.610
we've established that we can gather X Eggs simply by using a recording of the violin. {This shows as a three-liner for me, consider splitting at the comma}

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:26.750
Correct!

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:34.330
And with the new and improved Come Here Embryo Mk. II, we can make gobs of children hear it!

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.080
So just by doing that...

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.670
...we can extract a ton of X Eggs!

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.110
Okay back there?

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.760
Be careful!

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:49.700
What, it's my fault?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.020
Of course it is!

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:06.710
There, there...

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:28.580
Nagihiko, what are you doing?

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:31.270
Shh! The sports club kids are...

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:32.840
The baseball team is gonna get Fujisaki!

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:34.560
No way, it's gonna be the soccer team!

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.370
Volleyball!

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:36.100
Judo!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.450
But the basketball team had our eyes on him first!

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.150
Wow, it's really gotten out of control.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.240
Honestly... This is all your fault, Rhythm!

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.800
I know.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.630
But I've got a plan!

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:58.410
Hey, guys! I'll join the club of whoever catches me before I exit the school building!

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.290
Nagihiko?

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.890
Or wait, Rhythm?

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.500
Let's go!

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.110
W-Why?

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.760
What a shame! Game, set!

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:25.810
Put me down!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.310
I so totally suck.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:33.060
I can't believe I got you involved, Amu-chan...

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:35.410
Hey, it's okay. Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.570
Amu's totally right!

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:38.740
I don't wanna hear that from <i>you</i>!

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:42.400
Amu-chan's laughing at me...

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.250
I'm not.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:48.510
You're just always so calm and considerate,

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:53.480
it made me think of how rare it is to see you worried and depressed, Nagihiko.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:57.190
I guess Rhythm's thrown me for a bit of a loop.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:09:00.940
Nagihiko, you think about things too much.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.670
You should just join a club.

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:04.890
Which one?

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:05.720
All of 'em!

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:08.900
Now look here, I'm only one person, you know.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:13.750
And besides, being a Guardian keeps me busy, so it'd be too much.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.620
But it'd be fun, right?

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.680
That's not the issue.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.520
Isn't it, though?

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:22.000
Kukai!

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.040
You came to hang out again?

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.720
It's not becoming a habit! {literally "Don't say "again!""}

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.860
Yaya told me Fujisaki's Guardian Character was born, so I came to greet him, is all.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:32.940
Yo! I'm Daichi!

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.490
Nice to meet you, Rhythm.

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.750
Yay!

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:37.640
Hey, he's seems like a nice guy!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:43.510
I wouldn't say he's bad, but I do wish he'd think a bit before he acts.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:47.290
There are two types of Guardian Characters:

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:53.580
The ones born when you're already satisfied with yourself, but craving change,

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:57.190
and then the ones born from what you feel you lack.

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:01.870
So Rhythm is the type that compensates for something you lack, Fujisaki?

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:08.220
C-Cool... {P.S. I think this is a horrible horrible joke... Cool is "Ku-ru", but "Kuru" also can mean "to spin" as in what his eyes are doing}

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:15.510
I don't think I really want to act without careful thought, though...

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:19.130
But that's not Rhythm's only characteristic, right?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:21.880
What else is there?

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:24.440
He's very friendly.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:26.100
And enthusiastic, I'd say.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.060
And a total flirt.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:32.690
When you put it all together, all I can see is that he acts impulsively.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:38.290
W-Well, he was just born, so you haven't been together very long.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.820
Yeah! You'll understand him one day, for sure!

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:42.700
Bala-Balance!

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.450
You're good!

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:49.920
Wow! He can actually do "Bala-Balance" well enough to impress Kusukusu-dechu!

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.410
Bala-Balance!

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.590
My turn!

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.210
Bala-Balance!

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.970
What a show-off!

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.950
I guess Nagihiko is having problems adjusting to Rhythm.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.090
You were no different, Amu-chan.

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:28.810
You were shocked and angry and stuff when we were born, too, remember?

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.730
Now that you mention it, yeah.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:33.540
I'm sure they'll get along great in no time.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.180
Yeah.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.310
Ah, sorry!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.180
Are you okay?

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.240
Are you hurt?

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.500
Where's your mom and dad?

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.520
Were you together?

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:56.310
Can he see Guardian Characters?

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:01.000
Here ya go! Freshly baked!

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.700
Thank you!

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:06.120
Oh, he was looking at the taiyaki stand.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.480
Want some taiyaki?

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:16.420
My treat, since I bumped into you.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.180
Eat it while it's still hot, got it?

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:20.280
A baked fish?

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:24.030
Wait, have you never eaten taiyaki before?

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:26.340
This is a snack!

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.790
There's sweet bean paste on the inside!

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.850
You bite into it, like this!

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.560
A snack?

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:38.390
Do you not like sweet bean paste?

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.560
Don't force yourself, then, it's okay.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:49.170
He likes it, Miki!  {I'm referencing the classic commercial for life cereal :) (He likes it, Mikey!) Yeah, I think you'd have to be my age to get the reference...}

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:50.580
Thank goodness.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.600
I'm glad he's going at it so heartily.  {this and the next line are a bit of a translation trick... she's making the connection between Hikaru (that's the boys name, I believe, although in this script he is called "Taiyaki boy"), and Nagihiko... but I needed to use an expression that applies both to eating and to the more generic concept of Nagihiko doing things all-out, so I connected the two with "heart", to keep the literary flow but also maintain some semblence of natural english...}

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:57.090
Going at it with all your heart, huh?  {this is her thinking about Rhythm and Nagihiko}

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:58.000
Do you like it?

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:05.860
What a mysterious kid.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:08.300
That sound!

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:20.250
Okay! Come on out, all you little X Eggs! {he says "batsu tama-chan"... usually I don't translate -chan but in this context "X Egg-chan" reads very awkward}

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:25.690
I can't hear it anymore.

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:27.560
But we definitely heard it, right?

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:28.550
Yeah.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:32.330
He's gone.

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:34.270
Where did he go?

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:36.280
How mysterious.

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:39.260
Listen to me!

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.950
We're not a newspaper recycling truck!  {Perhaps an explanation is in order... For a number of services in Japan, they still do a very old tradition of driving slowly along the street, and stopping periodically and playing some sort of melody/announcement on a loudspeaker to announcer their presence, and then the housewives from the neighborhood would go and buy things/dispose of things at the truck etc...  Newspaper recycling (in older cities), electronic waste disposal, Yaki-imo trucks, tofu salesman (they have a very distinct horn they blow... There's one in my neighborhood that comes by everyday at like 5 PM), etc... }

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:45.440
You aren't? But you played that strange music, didn't you?

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.220
Strange?

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.010
This isn't working very well.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:56.250
We need a ton of people to hear it, not this rinky-dink number...

00:13:57.470 --> 00:14:04.440
It is now 5 o'clock. To everyone playing in the park: please watch out for cars on your way home.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:05.740
Eureka!  {I'm pretty sure this is a direct reference to archemidese (in translation, at least)}

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.570
Bye-bye, Mister!

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.070
Climb a tree again for us sometime!

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:13.500
Okay!

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:17.230
Rhythm...

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:19.260
You really need to be friendlier, Nagihiko.

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:20.860
Now, look here...

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.620
That sound...

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:33.740
At this rate, my place as King will be usurped by that Rhythm!

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:36.290
You worry about strange things, Kiseki.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:41.230
It's from Fujisaki-kun.  {wow, what a lame ring-tone.}

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:44.860
Hotori-kun, gather the others quickly and come to the park!

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:53.780
Taking over the park speaker was a great idea, Manta-kun! {note "taking over" and its use in the line a couple before are purposefully symmetrical.  Maintain this. Must we? :( I like usurped but it doesn't fit in this line! ;_;}

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:58.310
It got us quick results!

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:04.730
Rhythm!

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:05.630
Okay!

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:11.390
My heart: Unlock!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:30.270
Character Transformation: Beat Jumper!

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.910
It's Nagi's Character Transformation!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:41.350
Split into two groups, guys!

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:44.500
Yaya-chan and Rima-chan, you two search for the source of the sound.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:47.270
Roger! Let's go, Rima-tan!

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:49.070
Yaya!

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:52.760
Hotori-kun and Amu-chan, purify the X Eggs together!

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:53.710
Right!

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:56.210
Tadase, why are you letting yourself be ordered around?

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:58.320
It's fine. Let's Character Transform.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:15:59.390
Us, too!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.810
Pick me this time, please!

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.130
I wanna do it together with Rhythm... {ah, man, the double entrendre is SO thick!}

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:09.640
My heart:

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:10.780
My heart:

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.450
Unlock!

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:34.150
Character Transformation: Platinum Royal!

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:39.100
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:42.380
Let's go!

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:43.140
Right!

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.460
Holy Crown!

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:57.910
Colorful Canvas!

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:10.800
Come on, come out, come 'ere!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.130
That's...

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.010
Crap, they found us!

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.340
You can't escape!

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:24.940
Stop hiding and get out here!

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:29.480
Yaya, over there.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.350
We're outta here!

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:34.240
Hey! Get back here!

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:35.920
Yaya, look.

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:40.090
There are even more X Eggs than before.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:48.540
As I thought.

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:50.930
It's moving too fast, I can't hit it!

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:52.350
Three seconds!

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:57.510
That X Egg stops at three second intervals to make its attack.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.890
Aim for it then!

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:00.970
That's our Nagihiko!

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.470
One!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:06.230
Two!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.020
Three!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.360
Colorful Canvas!

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.120
All right!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.950
It repelled it?

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:29.830
Now it's even faster than before!

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.660
What should I do?

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:35.300
You're not gonna make it if you keep stressing about it.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.720
That's easy for you to say!

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.630
Ride the beat!

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:40.980
Just beat your rhythm into it!

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.620
But how?

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:45.100
Don't think, jump!

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:53.610
Fine, have it your way.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.860
Feel the beat!  {I've obviously added a bit here, to make it cooler...}

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.540
Ride the rhythm!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.310
March to the beat of my own drum!  {literally it's all one sentence that "means" (and I use the term lightly since it's frankly nonsense)  "I'm going to the beat, the rhythm, at my own pace!"}

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:11.500
Do it!

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:17.000
Beat Dunk!

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:28.350
Wow...

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:29.910
Now, Amu-chan!

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:30.730
Right!

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:37.070
Platinum Heart!

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:08.150
You did it, Nagihiko!

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:11.550
Rhythm, you were really cool.

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:13.190
Halt, commoners!

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:16.640
Rhythm wasn't the only one to lend aid!

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:20.070
I, the King, purified the X Eggs with Tadase, did I not?

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:21.940
We <i>know</i>.

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:26.120
If you have to go out of your way to point it out, you clearly aren't very capable.

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:27.990
What did you say?

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:35.480
You're the King, right?

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:37.070
Chill out!

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:38.940
Why you...

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:40.300
Yay!  {awwwwwww!  sorry, this surprised even me.... Rhythm isn't a playboy! He's just "simple" :) }

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:43.180
Yay?

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:54.840
You've got a pretty sweet groove goin' on yourself, Kiseki.

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:56.550
You think?

00:20:56.550 --> 00:21:00.000
Seems everyone's just falling right into Rhythm's pace.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.860
But thanks to him, you can do a lot of things you normally wouldn't, right?

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:05.490
I guess so, but...

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:11.250
I think I can understand throwing yourself into things instead of overthinking them.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.870
It's like taking a big bite out of a taiyaki.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.460
Taiyaki?

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:17.040
Yo!

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:20.130
Today was awesome! Yay!

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:23.800
Yay!

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.590
Follow me, Nagi!

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:31.020
Wait, Rhythm!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:34.980
You're back!

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:40.860
The ingredients in taiyaki are eggs, flour, water, and sugar made from adzuki beans.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.900
Don't think about it so much.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.740
Isn't it enough just to know it tastes good?

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:53.670
It's a completely pointless food containing too much sugar and carbohydrates.

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:55.250
That much I know.

00:21:56.740 --> 00:22:01.070
Snacks are not a necessary part of life.

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:14.370
Hey, Amu-chi! We're going home! Amu-chi!

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:32.950
You sure do seem determined.

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:39.000
So even if you screw up, it'll somehow turn out all right.

00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:46.370
How about you just trust in yourself?

00:22:46.650 --> 00:22:52.830
Take that first step and everything will work out fine.

00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:59.760
Even if people see through your cool exterior, keep marching on.

00:23:00.180 --> 00:23:08.840
Look up at the blue sky and everything will reset!

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:12.480
Take it easy! Take it easy!  {the first is in English, the second is in Japanese (but that is the exact same meaning)}

00:23:12.760 --> 00:23:23.020
Try to relax those shoulders and clear your mind.

00:23:23.020 --> 00:23:29.730
The more you do it, the easier it'll get, so keep taking it easy.

00:23:29.730 --> 00:23:34.930
Ride the flow of time and you'll be...

00:23:35.990 --> 00:23:38.730
Shining! Shining! Shining!

00:23:50.150 --> 00:23:54.530
Amu-chan, I hear Utau-chan's new song is finally done!

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:55.510
What's it like?

00:23:55.510 --> 00:23:57.860
You can look forward to that next time!

00:23:57.860 --> 00:23:59.290
Next time on Shugo Chara-

00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:00.240
Don't jump the gun!

00:24:00.240 --> 00:24:03.210
She also said she's finally doing a concert.

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:05.080
Great! Then we should all go cheer her on!

00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:07.720
It's a perfect plot, to make her concert rock! {okay, now I'm just being silly... my heart of a poet seeps out sometimes}

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:09.420
Is it time to go yet?

00:24:09.730 --> 00:24:11.980
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki:

00:24:11.980 --> 00:24:14.200
Hoshina Utau, Fly to the Future!

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:16.260
We're countin' on you all!

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.930
We'll never forgive you for missing it!
